<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmad al-Muqtadir</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1081</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Ahmad I al-Muqtadir</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmad al-Muqtadir (died 1081) was the Hudid king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">Taifa</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a> from 1046 and its most powerful ruler. He removed his brothers from their shares of the kingdom, annexed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tortosa">Tortosa</a> around 1060 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denia">Dénia</a> in 1076, and paid tribute to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> while fighting Aragon, notably at Graus in 1063, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramiro-i-of-aragon">Ramiro I of Aragon</a> was killed. He built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aljaferia">Aljafería</a> palace in Zaragoza.</p></div>
